    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ds0x86j",
      "content": "Engineering drawing is the graphical language used by engineers and technicians to communicate ideas, designs, and technical information. It represents objects, machines, and structures using lines, symbols, dimensions, and standardized conventions. Engineering drawings are essential in manufacturing, construction, maintenance, and technical trades such as fitting, machining, and electrical work."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cdyx3s8",
      "content": "In technical trades, engineering drawings help workers understand the exact shape, size, and assembly of machine parts. Accurate drawings ensure that components are manufactured and assembled correctly."
    },
    {
      "id": "2o14lsk",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Importance of Engineering Drawing"
    },
    {
      "id": "a6fwu9i",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Communicates technical information clearly",
        "Shows exact dimensions and shapes of components",
        "Helps in manufacturing and assembly of parts",
        "Reduces errors in production",
        "Provides a permanent technical record",
        "Used as a universal language for engineers and technicians"
      ]
    },
