    {
      "id": "23n97wo",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Dimensioning in Engineering Drawing"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wxi4f5i",
      "content": "Dimensioning is the process of indicating the size and location of features on a drawing. It provides numerical values for length, diameter, radius, and angles."
    },
    {
      "id": "05i583i",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Dimensions should be clear and easy to read",
        "Do not repeat dimensions unnecessarily",
        "Dimension lines should not cross each other",
        "Arrowheads should touch the extension lines",
        "Units are usually in millimetres unless specified"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "zy46gn7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Orthographic Projection"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gld8aq1",
      "content": "Orthographic projection is a method of representing a three-dimensional object using two-dimensional views. Each view shows the object from a different direction."
    },
    {
      "id": "j4pepal",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>View</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Description</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Front View</p>",
            "<p>Shows height and width</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Top View (Plan)</p>",
            "<p>Shows width and depth</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Side View</p>",
            "<p>Shows height and depth</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1n0buip",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Lettering in Engineering Drawing"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gjr7mim",
      "content": "Lettering is used to write titles, notes, dimensions, and labels on drawings. Good lettering should be uniform, clear, and easy to read."
    },
    {
      "id": "toqt5e1",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Letters should be evenly spaced",
        "Use capital letters for clarity",
        "Maintain uniform height and thickness",
        "Use standard lettering styles"
      ]
    },
